# Size-frequency docking: current authoring decisions

Canonical: monochromatic 8-connected components; modal background; equal occupied-cell counts, not shape/color equality. Sizes occurring at least twice move to the top; singleton sizes move to the bottom, without horizontal displacement. All four supplied labels (including two test golds) are authoring checks, not unseen evaluation.

Alternate `bridge_top`: first dock exactly as canonical, then fill background gaps between the leftmost and rightmost occupied top-edge cells with 9 (0 on a 9 background). The top-edge occupancy is created by the repeated-size decision. `wrong_intermediate.rkt` preserves the correctly docked canvas but derives the bridge anchors from the original top edge. Its counterfactual difference therefore isolates stage B rather than merely moving the singleton objects incorrectly.

Sampler: independently grown irregular 8-connected animals, distinct shapes, shared colors across size classes, 2–6 demonstrations, four distinct size-profile queries, matched input streams. The first two demos swap which area is repeated. Six-object 30×30 queries span the canvas; morphology remains intentionally sparse like the originals. Input/output collisions are excluded by separating columns.

Plan: original-label and literal behavior tests first; implement both rules; replay protected Racket; audit named shortcuts, counts and public isolation; repair concrete findings; preflight exact final sources; relocated replay; return source delta. No source registration, owner acceptance, or training admission is claimed.

Self-review repairs: seeds 18 and 28 exposed bounding-box-area and 4-connectivity shortcuts respectively. Both concrete old lessons were confirmed with protected Racket (two demonstrations fit, query fails). Demo zero now contrasts a solid bar with an equal-area animal carrying a diagonal-only terminal; their bounding-box areas differ. This constructively exposes occupied-cell count and 8-connectivity without adding demonstrations. Public verifier also rejects symlinks and non-JSON sidecars after observed negative-test failures.
